-134332390,imgsize-267892.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[37 miners found dead in Nigerian paramilitary custody, sparking protests]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134331364.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/37-miners-found-dead-in-nigerian-paramilitary-custody-sparking-protests/articleshow/134331364.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/37-miners-found-dead-in-nigerian-paramilitary-custody-sparking-protests/articleshow/134331364.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T15:38:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134332069,imgsize-91810.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Charlie Puth’s $4.17M Montecito home sells for $18.5M after 9 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134331811.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a noteworthy real estate move, Charlie Puth has divested his Montecito estate for a stunning eighteen point five million dollars, significantly higher than his 2017 acquisition cost of four point one seven million dollars. This charming residence holds cherished memories, including his marriage to Brooke Sansone two years ago. This transaction showcases Puth's impressive financial progression, complementing his recent California property sales.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2017-charlie-puth-paid-4-17-million-for-a-montecito-home-where-he-later-married-brooke-sansone-nine-years-later-the-5920-sq-ft-property-sold-off-market-for-18-5-million/articleshow/134331811.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2017-charlie-puth-paid-4-17-million-for-a-montecito-home-where-he-later-married-brooke-sansone-nine-years-later-the-5920-sq-ft-property-sold-off-market-for-18-5-million/articleshow/134331811.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T15:36:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134332001,imgsize-323544.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US journalist vanished in Syria 14 years ago; now his driver’s shocking betrayal is revealed]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134329387.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Austin Tice, a journalist, disappeared in Syria in 2012 while covering the civil war.  New BBC findings suggest his driver betrayed him to the Syrian regime for rewards.  Confidential intelligence files indicate the Syrian government detained Tice after his alleged abduction.  His mother maintains he is alive and being treated well by his captors.  The US government continues its active investigation and offers a reward for his return.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/14-years-after-he-vanished-a-shocking-betrayal-may-reveal-what-happened-to-us-journalist-austin-tice-in-syria/articleshow/134329387.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/14-years-after-he-vanished-a-shocking-betrayal-may-reveal-what-happened-to-us-journalist-austin-tice-in-syria/articleshow/134329387.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T15:44:16+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134329872,imgsize-728190.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Watch: Chinese coast guard vessel rams civilian Philippine boat in South China Sea]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134331498.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a troubling turn of events, a Chinese Coast Guard ship collided with a boat from the Philippine Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources while it was refueling local fishermen. Although the Philippine vessel sustained structural damage, no injuries were reported. China claims that the Philippine boat ignored warnings and changed its course, further escalating tensions in the already contentious South China Sea.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/chinese-coast-guard-vessel-rams-civilian-philippine-boat-on-refuelling-mission-in-south-china-sea/articleshow/134331498.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/chinese-coast-guard-vessel-rams-civilian-philippine-boat-on-refuelling-mission-in-south-china-sea/articleshow/134331498.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T15:27:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134331702,imgsize-50660.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Carrine Meyrignac built her company in Los Angeles garage with $30,000; it grew to $5 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134331404.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Carinne Meyrignac founded Cali's Books after noticing a gap in musical children's books. She invested thirty thousand dollars in her initial book order from China. Direct-to-consumer sales proved crucial for the company's significant growth. Cali's Books achieved one million dollars in revenue by the year 2020. The business later reached five million dollars in revenue by 2024.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/she-started-a-childrens-book-company-from-her-los-angeles-garage-with-30000-it-grew-to-5-million-in-annual-revenue/articleshow/134331404.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/she-started-a-childrens-book-company-from-her-los-angeles-garage-with-30000-it-grew-to-5-million-in-annual-revenue/articleshow/134331404.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T15:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134331474,imgsize-973321.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[12-year-old rescued 114 thrift-store stuffed toys, repaired each by hand and gave them to fire victims]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134328805.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a heartwarming initiative, a young girl from North Carolina took it upon herself to collect discarded stuffed animals from local thrift shops. After cleaning and lovingly restoring 114 toys, she donated them to children affected by home loss due to a fire. This project not only offered solace to struggling children but also emphasized the importance of recycling and giving toys a new lease on life.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-12-year-old-north-carolina-girl-rescued-114-stuffed-animals-from-thrift-stores-she-repaired-every-one-by-hand-and-donated-them-to-children-who-lost-their-homes-in-fire/articleshow/134328805.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-12-year-old-north-carolina-girl-rescued-114-stuffed-animals-from-thrift-stores-she-repaired-every-one-by-hand-and-donated-them-to-children-who-lost-their-homes-in-fire/articleshow/134328805.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T15:07:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134329102,imgsize-1309167.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA